\f0\fs24 \cf0 Transcriptome Day 3 - April 30,2026\
\
Step 1) Generate Volcano Plot.\
Determine the extent to which genes are up- or down-regulated using a volcano plot.\
Tool: Volcano Plot\
Version: Galaxy Version 4.0.2+galaxy0\
Parameters: Input differential gene expression file. \'93FDR (adjusted P value) column number\'94 should be set to column 7, \'93P value (raw) column number\'94 set to column 6, \'93Log Fold Change column number\'94 set to column 3, \'93Labels column number\'94 set to column 1. All other parameters set to default.\
Notes: To interpret the volcano plot, points plotted along the y-axis represent the P value (indicator of significance). The x-axis indicates whether there was up-regulation or down-regulation. The further left the point is means there is down-regulation and the further right the point is means there was up-regulation.\
\
Step 2) Look at the top 10 up- and 10 down-regulated genes.\
Focus only on the top 10 up-regulated and top 10 down-regulated genes by remove all other genes in the table file.\
Tool: Excel\
Version: 16.108.1\
Parameters: Sorted data by log scale fold change, selected both the top 10 up- and down-regulated genes (total of 20). Saved into new .csv file\
Notes: This new top 10 up- and down- file should be uploaded to galaxy. Then need to convert to tabular by selecting \'93Edit Attributes\'94, then go to the \'93Datatypes\'94 tab, and select \'93tabular\'94 instead of \'93text\'94.\
\
